Here is the complete, in-order breakdown of the `POST /api/owners` code path. I read every file in the chain; no `@PrePersist`/lifecycle callbacks, entity listeners, or published events exist anywhere in `src/` (verified by grep).

## 1. Controller method (verbatim)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` — class is a `@RestController` with `@RequestMapping("/api")` (lines 52-55). The mapping/`@Valid`/`@RequestBody` come from the generated `OwnersApi` interface it implements.

Method, lines 104-115:
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    this.ownerRequestValidator.validate(ownerFieldsDto);
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

The actual HTTP mapping + `@Valid` is defined on the interface method it overrides — `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`, lines 79-87:
```java
@RequestMapping(method = RequestMethod.POST, value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER, /* "/owners" */
    produces = { "application/json" }, consumes = { "application/json" })
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(...required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
) { ... }
```

## 2. Request DTO + Bean Validation annotations

The request body binds to `OwnerFieldsDto` (NOT the `Owner` entity). File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java`. Constraints are on the getters:

- `firstName` (line 62): `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName` (line 83): `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `address` (line 104): `@NotNull` `@Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `city` (line 125): `@NotNull` `@Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- `telephone` (line 146): `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]*$")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 20)`

No class-level constraints, no validation groups, no custom constraint annotations on the DTO.

Note the `Owner` **entity** also carries Bean Validation annotations, but these only fire if the persistence provider validates on flush (not explicitly triggered in this path). `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`:
- `address` (line 39) `@NotEmpty`; `city` (line 43) `@NotEmpty`; `telephone` (lines 47-49) `@NotEmpty` `@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)` `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")`.
- Inherited from `Person` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java` lines 31-37): `firstName` `@NotEmpty`, `lastName` `@NotEmpty`.

## 3. Custom validator (second validation layer)

`this.ownerRequestValidator.validate(...)` is called explicitly at controller line 107, BEFORE mapping/saving. File `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/OwnerRequestValidator.java`, lines 41-59:
```java
public void validate(OwnerFieldsDto owner) {
    Map<String, String> requiredFields = new LinkedHashMap<>();
    requiredFields.put("firstName", owner.getFirstName());
    requiredFields.put("lastName", owner.getLastName());
    requiredFields.put("address", owner.getAddress());
    requiredFields.put("city", owner.getCity());
    requiredFields.put("telephone", owner.getTelephone());
    List<String> missingFields = new ArrayList<>();
    requiredFields.forEach((name, value) -> {
        if (!StringUtils.hasText(value)) { missingFields.add(name); }
    });
    if (!missingFields.isEmpty()) {
        throw new RequiredFieldsMissingException(missingFields);
    }
}
```
It re-checks the same 5 fields for null/empty/blank (`StringUtils.hasText`) in insertion order and throws `RequiredFieldsMissingException` naming every offending field. This is redundant with the `@NotNull`/`@Size` on the DTO but is a distinct, explicit check. No uniqueness check, no normalization, no defaults — it is purely a presence check.

## 4. Mapper (DTO -> entity)

`ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` (controller line 109). Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` lines 25-27 — `@Mapping(target = "id", ignore = true)` and `@Mapping(target = "pets", ignore = true)`.

Generated impl `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/annotations/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapperImpl.java` lines 62-77: straight field copy of firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone into a new `Owner`. No trimming, casing, or other normalization. `id` and `pets` left null.

## 5. Service + repository (the save / side-effects)

`this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (controller line 110). Impl `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` lines 232-237:
```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```
No business rules, no uniqueness check, no default-setting, no password hashing (owners have no credentials), no timestamps. Just a transactional passthrough to `ownerRepository.save`. `@Transactional` here opens the transaction.

Repository is Spring Data JPA: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` — `save` is the inherited default `JpaRepository`/`CrudRepository.save` (no custom override; only finders are customized). Persist assigns the id via `@GeneratedValue(strategy = IDENTITY)` on `BaseEntity` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java` lines 33-35). No `@PrePersist`.

(There are also `jpa` and `jdbc` profile implementations of `OwnerRepository` under `.../repository/jpa` and `.../repository/jdbc`; which one is active depends on the Spring profile. The `spring-data-jpa` one above is the default in this project.)

## 6. Response side-effects

After save (controller lines 111-114): `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` maps entity back to `OwnerDto` (includes now-populated `id` and empty `pets` list), a `Location` header `/api/owners/{id}` is set, and `201 CREATED` is returned.

## Exception handlers relevant to creation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` (`@ControllerAdvice`):
- `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (lines 133-169) → 400, builds a `ProblemDetail` with `errors` (distinct field names) and `schemaValidationErrors` list. This catches the DTO `@Valid` failures from step 2.
- `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (lines 179-190) → 400, sets `errors` property to `e.getMissingFields()`. Catches the custom validator from step 3.
- `DataIntegrityViolationException` (lines 113-124) → 404 (DB constraint violations on save).
- `AccessDeniedException` (lines 84-87) re-thrown so Security produces 403/entry-point (relevant to the `@PreAuthorize`).
- `Exception` catch-all (lines 96-103) → 500.

## Full execution order for a POST /api/owners

1. Spring MVC deserializes the JSON body into `OwnerFieldsDto`.
2. `@Valid` (OwnersApi line 86) triggers Bean Validation on the DTO during argument resolution — the `@NotNull` / `@Size` / `@Pattern` constraints in section 2. Failure → `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400.
3. Method-security `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` (controller line 104) enforces the `OWNER_ADMIN` role on method invocation. Failure → `AccessDeniedException` → 403.
4. `ownerRequestValidator.validate(dto)` (line 107) — explicit presence re-check of firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone in that order. Failure → `RequiredFieldsMissingException` → 400.
5. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` (line 109) — copy 5 fields into a new `Owner`; id and pets ignored/null. No normalization.
6. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (line 110) — opens `@Transactional`, calls `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; JPA INSERT, id generated via IDENTITY. No business/uniqueness/default/timestamp logic. DB constraint failure → `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404.
7. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` (line 111) — map saved entity (now with id) back to `OwnerDto`.
8. Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header (lines 112-113) and return `201 CREATED` (line 114).

There are no emails, audit logs, published events, related-entity creation, or password hashing anywhere in this path.

